<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lake Smolino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1502</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Smolina · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscovite-lithuanian-war-1500-1503">Muscovite–Lithuanian War (1500–1503)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Lake Smolino was fought on 13 September 1502 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pskov">Pskov</a>, when the Livonian Order under Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolter-von-plettenberg">Wolter von Plettenberg</a> defeated a much larger Muscovite army. Fought during the Muscovite–Lithuanian War of 1500–1503, in which the order was allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, the victory led to a truce in 1503 and kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> free of Russian invasion for decades.</p></div>
